[h1]Project Vigilance: Overland Incursions &amp; Geoscape Strategy[/h1]
[b]Replaces instantaneous map-edge teleportation with physical overland planetary transit, dynamic multi-vector staging, early-warning radar networks, multi-dish interferometry, drifting orbital satellites, lightweight listening posts, and tactical ground interception.[/b]
No high-tech requirements. Zero prerequisites. Safe to add mid-save.
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Key Features[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]Campaign Creation Wizard &amp; Mutability (New in v0.4):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Integrated campaign wizard page stitched between Storyteller and World settings with 4 gameplay profiles: [i]Classic Fog of War[/i] (recommended default), [i]Planetary Surveillance[/i], [i]Hardcore Vigilance[/i], and [i]Omniscient[/i].
    [*] Granular rule customisation modal allowing players to configure fog behavior, caravan sight, incursion staging, and radar power scaling.
    [*] Blind Touchdown: Landing site selection under Fog of War masks unviable mountain/ocean drops and Biotech pollution/climate warnings so you land blind into the uncharted rimworld.
    [*] Cryptographic HMAC-SHA256 audit ledger tracking rule transitions, escalations, and settings history.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Planetary Radar Infrastructure &amp; Multi-Dish Interferometry (New in v0.4):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Native 3D glowing perimeter boundaries and hexagonal honeycomb radar meshes projected directly onto the planetary globe.
    [*] New colony sensory structures across tech tiers: [i]Lookout Tower[/i] (Neolithic/Medieval), [i]Early-Warning Radar Dome[/i] (Industrial), [i]Spacer Phased Array[/i], and [i]SIGINT Decryption Console[/i].
    [*] Dynamic power scaling: radars consume minimal standby power until scanning or actively tracking contacts.
    [*] Multi-dish stacking: secondary dishes expand optical identification horizons outward (from 10 rings up to 22 rings) with built-in fail-safe redundancy.
    [*] Model B+ Vantage &amp; Terrain Masking: Hill/mountain origins boost lookout vantage, while rugged mountains delay classification until incursions exit into open valleys (penetrated by Spacer Phased Arrays + SIGINT).
    [/list]
[*] [b]Unmanned Listening Posts &amp; Signal Beacons (New in v0.4):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Deploy unmanned solar listening relays and stone/wood signal beacons directly from travelling caravans via right-click global hex interaction.
    [*] Dismantle outposts at any time to recover 75% of consumed construction materials.
    [*] Repair sabotaged stations damaged by passing hostile warbands.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Two-Stage Early Warning &amp; Concealed Haze Sites (New in v0.4):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Two-stage alert escalation: Stage 1 outer perimeter warning (pulsing amber contact blip, concealed faction/threat) transitioning to Stage 2 upon crossing the optical classification threshold.
    [*] Haze of War site concealment: dynamic camps, quest sites, and bandit outposts in unmonitored sectors remain hidden until charted by radar sweeps, scout caravans, or traveller rumors.
    [*] Quest expiration timers are paused while sites remain shrouded in the Haze.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Simulated Inter-Faction Encounters &amp; Trade Routes (New in v0.4):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Organic NPC trade network: physical NPC caravans travel between faction settlements with genuine cargo rosters.
    [*] Grounded storyteller caravan meetings and ambushes physically march across the world map.
    [*] Algebraic background skirmishes resolve in-flight clashes between rival forces occupying the same tile without tactical map lag.
    [*] Spawns persistent battlefield aftermath sites containing salvageable trade loot and wounded survivor pawns.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Drifting Keplerian Orbital Logistics &amp; Trade Satellites (New in v0.4):[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Physically consistent analytical Keplerian flight model with J2 planetary oblateness nodal precession, creating smoothly drifting ground tracks across planetary longitudes.
    [*] Persistent Orbital Station hubs for orbital factions (such as Trader's Guild / Merchant's Bazaar).
    [*] Dedicated trade satellites with periodic comms console trading windows and drop pod cargo delivery.
    [*] Dual-layer rendering across surface and Odyssey orbit views with dynamic faction livery color tinting.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Real-Time Planetary Transit:[/b] Raids, trade caravans, and visitors spawn at genuine world origin settlements or wilderness staging camps and march across the globe in real time.
[*] [b]Tactical Ground Interception &amp; Forward Ambush:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Intercept approaching hostile incursions directly on the global hex grid before they reach your colony.
    [*] Right-click commands on detected incursions: [i]Intercept &amp; Engage[/i], [i]Hail &amp; Trade[/i], or [i]Warn Away / Turn Back[/i].
    [*] Stalk unaware enemy columns or launch daring night ambushes while hostile warbands are camped asleep.
    [*] Intercepting caravans dynamically adjust course with predictive pursuit vectoring as their quarry moves.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Retreat Lifecycle, Pursuit &amp; Kidnap Recovery:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Fleeing raiders physically retreat across the world map with wounds, carried loot, and captured colonists intact.
    [*] Overland physiology: wounded marchers bleed, heal, self-tend with carried medicine, or suffer exhaustion.
    [*] Intercept retreating kidnappers on the road to rescue captured colonists before they reach home territory—or mount a base assault on their stronghold to liberate prisoners from settlement incarceration!
    [*] Threat-aware tactical retreats: fleeing colonists evaluate visible enemies, turrets, and fire exposure across all map boundaries to pick the safest evacuation corridor.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Evacuated Colony Hierarchy &amp; Track Pursuit:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Hostile forces reaching an evacuated player colony or abandoned settlement don't disappear into thin air.
    [*] Raiders execute a 3-tier tactical hierarchy: search for tracks and launch dynamic hot pursuit after fleeing player caravans, divert toward nearby secondary outposts, or ransack the vacant site and march home.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Night Owl &amp; Schedule-Aware Caravaning:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Caravans respect colonist traits and timetable schedules rather than enforcing rigid 22:00–06:00 sleep locks.
    [*] Pure Night Owl squads camp during the day (11:00–18:00) and march through the night with zero optical darkness penalties.
    [*] Mixed squads march by majority shift while keeping the other on camp watch—granting 24/7 daytime visibility.
    [*] Set custom sleep shifts or force-march through rest hours via the colonist [i]Schedule[/i] tab.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Pack Animal Cargo &amp; Roadside Trading:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Trade goods and provisions are carried in pack animal inventories across all battle maps and transits (no floor-dumping).
    [*] Barter with friendly travelling merchants directly on the road without duplicating stock upon colony arrival.
    [*] Trader loss lifecycle: surviving escort guards execute tactical withdrawals if their merchant falls.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Classic 3-Tier Haze of War:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] [i]Shrouded:[/i] Pitch-black mask over unmapped planetary tiles.
    [*] [i]Obscured:[/i] Surveyed world geography and settlements remain visible, but active incursions are hidden outside sensor coverage.
    [*] [i]Monitored:[/i] Full live sensory visibility projected by your colonies, outposts, and travelling caravans.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Watertight Information Security &amp; X-COM Tracking IDs:[/b] Approaching forces outside your immediate sight lines are designated with persistent tracking numbers ([i]Contact-1[/i], [i]Contact-2[/i] or [i]Approaching Strangers #1[/i] for tribals). Originating faction, threat points, and route overlays remain classified until scouted.
[*] [b]Dynamic Nighttime &amp; Sleep Simulation:[/b]
    [list]
    [*] Visual detection horizons drop by 50% during local planetary darkness.
    [*] Settlement lookouts collapse to a tight perimeter when all conscious colonists are asleep in bed.
    [*] Biological warbands and trade caravans stop and make camp between 22:00 and 06:00 local solar time, while tireless Mechanoid and Anomaly incursions march 24/7.
    [/list]
[*] [b]Configurable In-Game Settings:[/b] Customise settlement sight range, caravan vision, night reduction penalties, and march speed multipliers directly in Mod Options. Features a live CRT radar scope preview!
[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Compatibility &amp; Performance[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]DLC Compatibility:[/b] 100% compatible with the base game, as well as Royalty, Ideology, Biotech, Anomaly, and Odyssey.
[*] [b]Save Games:[/b] Safe to add to existing saves. Safe to remove (any in-flight world incursions will simply disband cleanly).
[*] [b]Era Agnostic:[/b] Fits seamlessly into neolithic, medieval, industrial, or spacer playthroughs.
[*] [b]Performance:[/b] Zero-allocation spatial bitmasks and time-sliced 3D mesh layers guarantee buttery-smooth 60+ FPS panning with zero TPS impact.
[/list]
[h2]Recommended Load Order[/h2]
[olist]
[*] Harmony
[*] Core
[*] All Official DLCs (optional)
[*] [b]Project Vigilance - Overland Incursions[/b]
[/olist]
[hr][/hr]
[h2]Reporting Bugs &amp; Feedback[/h2]
Have a bug report, suggestion, or feedback?
[list]
[*] [b]GitHub Issues (Preferred):[/b] [url=https://github.com/CTOUT/Project-Vigilance/issues]Report an Issue on GitHub[/url] — Recommended for fastest troubleshooting! Please include your debug log (via the in-game log window or [i]Player.log[/i]), RimWorld version, and steps to reproduce.
[*] [b]Steam Discussions &amp; Comments:[/b] If you prefer Steam, feel free to open a topic in our [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/discussions/3822378226]Workshop Discussions[/url] or leave a comment below. Please include error details or a log link whenever possible!
[/list]
